["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Tens of Thousands of Earthworks Under the Amazon, and a Civilization of Perhaps Three Million Using LiDAR to see through the rainforest canopy, archaeologists have found tens of thousands of earthworks in the southwestern Amazon, spread across more than 180,000 square kilometres, with a peak population that may have reached 3 million. Nature Podcast Nature Podcast Earthworks spotted in the Amazon hint at huge ancient civilization Amazon archaeology LiDAR Cephalopod fossils Fungal textiles Ancient civilizations Science findings LiDAR geoglyph siphuncle\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-29-naturepod-亚马逊地下古文明规模是预估的十倍/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/61b9f3b71a8cbe675f3cedcb/1768403592746-2c5f9e78-ae15-499a-9d0a-ae6ca82bb9ca.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">20:30</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Nature Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0729</span></div>\n<h2>Tens of Thousands of Earthworks Under the Amazon, and a Civilization of Perhaps Three Million</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Using LiDAR to see through the rainforest canopy, archaeologists have found tens of thousands of earthworks in the southwestern Amazon, spread across more than 180,000 square kilometres, with a peak population that may have reached 3 million.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Amazon archaeology</span><span class=\"tag\">LiDAR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Non-programmers Were Sneaking Into Codex, and ChatGPT Work Followed OpenAI handed knowledge workers the Codex harness essentially unchanged, altering only the UX trade-offs and the sandbox defaults. The judgment underneath: AI will erase the boundaries between job functions, so OpenAI refuses to draw product lines around &quot;who you are&quot;. Latent Space Latent Space Codex from 0 to 10M Users: Building ChatGPT Work — Akshay Nathan, OpenAI Agent product design Enterprise adoption Knowledge work Productivity metrics OpenAI harness artifacts Sites Chronicle at-bats OpenClaw\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-28-latentspace-chatgpt-work-与-codex-是同一个-harness-差的只是-u/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/1084089/post/208716574/785c77f3b1ee5df365a6ac3479929a6c.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:09:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Latent Space</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0728</span></div>\n<h2>Non-programmers Were Sneaking Into Codex, and ChatGPT Work Followed</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI handed knowledge workers the Codex harness essentially unchanged, altering only the UX trade-offs and the sandbox defaults. The judgment underneath: AI will erase the boundaries between job functions, so OpenAI refuses to draw product lines around &quot;who you are&quot;.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Agent product design</span><span class=\"tag\">Enterprise adoption</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Intelligence will commoditize like RAM; OpenAI&#x27;s real moat is compute Sam Altman takes stock: intelligence itself will commoditize the way RAM did, and the durable advantage is the ability to manufacture cheaper compute. He also walks through ChatGPT&#x27;s accidental birth, the Hugging Face safety incident, and how the bottleneck keeps moving. Invest Like the Best Invest Like the Best Sam Altman - How to Make an Abundant Future - [Invest Like the Best, EP.484] Compute OpenAI Model cycle ChatGPT origins Commoditized intelligence Robotics distillation zero-day exploit Pareto optimal frontier scaling laws\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-28-ilt-智能终将商品化-openai-真正的护城河是算力/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/aa5cce3c-879b-11f1-8b29-8bc127cc1ad0/image/9f938c702e39c92a9999e2b29ad60310.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">53:33</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Invest Like the Best</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0728</span></div>\n<h2>Intelligence will commoditize like RAM; OpenAI&#x27;s real moat is compute</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Sam Altman takes stock: intelligence itself will commoditize the way RAM did, and the durable advantage is the ability to manufacture cheaper compute. He also walks through ChatGPT&#x27;s accidental birth, the Hugging Face safety incident, and how the bottleneck keeps moving.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute</span><span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Open models will win, and vLLM is the Linux of AI inference vLLM is already the most active open-source project on GitHub, but Kaichao You&#x27;s (游凯超) real claim is this: model capability cannot stay hidden for long, open models will win in the end, and the inference engine is the next Linux — where the moat is fast iteration, not the model itself. 张小珺·商业访谈录 张小珺·商业访谈录 148. 对游凯超3小时访谈：开源Infra、和模型Co-design 、“如果vLLM失败，我们会后悔一辈子” Open source AI Infra vLLM Model inference Startups Co-design PagedAttention KV Cache Speculative Decoding MOE (Mixture of Experts) BYOC (Bring Your Own Cloud)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-28-zhangxiaojun-开源模型会赢-vllm-是-ai-推理的-linux/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/Ftbpq0Qo78T0CFfOAWBKOoem8hVn.png?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"张\"><span class=\"dur\">3:00:26</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">张小珺·商业访谈录</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0728</span></div>\n<h2>Open models will win, and vLLM is the Linux of AI inference</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">vLLM is already the most active open-source project on GitHub, but Kaichao You&#x27;s (<span lang=\"zh\">游凯超</span>) real claim is this: model capability cannot stay hidden for long, open models will win in the end, and the inference engine is the next Linux — where the moat is fast iteration, not the model itself.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Open source</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Infra</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"AI Won&#x27;t Break SAP, But It Will Break Per-Seat Pricing AI will not flatten what enterprise software has accumulated, but it will break the per-seat pricing model. SAP&#x27;s defense is not training its own foundation model — it is open partnership plus business understanding, and the real battlefield is the last mile: process, data and organizational inertia. 晚点聊 LateTalk 晚点聊 174: AI冲击企业软件巨头？与SAP原欣聊大模型to B的颠覆与边界 Enterprise Software SaaS Pricing AI for B2B FDE SAP Organizational Inertia ERP / Enterprise Resource Planning FDE / Forward Deployed Engineer Human in the loop Process mining Physical AI\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-27-latetalk-企业软件不会死-死的是按坐席收费的模式/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/1/19a49f52-28ee-4e25-b8e9-4f0ee70917e0/episodes/3/36e00501-28e2-47a2-9489-32bc7b788267/cover.jpg?v=1\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"晚\"><span class=\"dur\">1:31:43</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">晚点聊 LateTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0727</span></div>\n<h2>AI Won&#x27;t Break SAP, But It Will Break Per-Seat Pricing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI will not flatten what enterprise software has accumulated, but it will break the per-seat pricing model. SAP&#x27;s defense is not training its own foundation model — it is open partnership plus business understanding, and the real battlefield is the last mile: process, data and organizational inertia.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Enterprise Software</span><span class=\"tag\">SaaS Pricing</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Chinese superpods now out-compute NVIDIA in total, but 5x the power buys no ecosystem Huawei&#x27;s CloudMatrix 384 spends roughly 560 kW to deliver 1.7x the total compute of an NVL72, but what decides the fate of domestic superpods is not the spec sheet — it is manufacturing capacity and the software ecosystem. What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道 科技早知道 国产 AI 算力能凭「超节点」弯道超车吗? | WAIC 深度观察 S10E23 Compute Superpods Domestic chips AI infrastructure NVIDIA Scale-up Scale-out UALink / Ultra Accelerator Link CloudMatrix / Huawei&#x27;s superpod line\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-27-whatsnext-国产超节点总算力反超英伟达-但功耗翻五倍换不来生态/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/4/4931937e-0184-4c61-a658-6b03c254754d/cover.jpg?v=10\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"W\"><span class=\"dur\">47:23</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0727</span></div>\n<h2>Chinese superpods now out-compute NVIDIA in total, but 5x the power buys no ecosystem</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Huawei&#x27;s CloudMatrix 384 spends roughly 560 kW to deliver 1.7x the total compute of an NVL72, but what decides the fate of domestic superpods is not the spec sheet — it is manufacturing capacity and the software ecosystem.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute</span><span class=\"tag\">Superpods</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Without Claude Code, Opus 4.5 Would Never Have Had Its Breakout Anthropic&#x27;s product lead looks back: however strong a model gets, users only feel it through a vehicle like Claude Code — and the core of the PM job has shifted from writing PRDs to writing evals. As she puts it, the eval is the new PRD. Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Anthropic’s first technical PM on token maxing, the jagged edge, and living in the future | Dianne Penn Product Management AI Research Orgs Evals Anthropic Culture Frontier Model Safety Token Economics token maxing jagged edge evals DRI red teaming hive mind\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-26-lennys-没有claude-code-opus-4-5不会有那波爆发/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/10845/post/207214207/756e556fcbda393739f83e6d27dbbe52.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:33:50</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Lenny&#x27;s Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0726</span></div>\n<h2>Without Claude Code, Opus 4.5 Would Never Have Had Its Breakout</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Anthropic&#x27;s product lead looks back: however strong a model gets, users only feel it through a vehicle like Claude Code — and the core of the PM job has shifted from writing PRDs to writing evals. As she puts it, the eval is the new PRD.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Product Management</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Research Orgs</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"China Cut 5 Million Barrels a Day of Imports — Why the Iran Oil Apocalypse Never Came The Iran war was once forecast to push oil to $200 a barrel; the disaster never arrived, and the main reason was not the United States but China quietly cutting crude imports by 5 million barrels a day — discretion that can rescue a market, and can just as easily be turned into a geopolitical weapon. ChinaTalk ChinaTalk The Iran War Oil Shock That Wasn’t...(Yet?) Energy security US-China rivalry Strategic Petroleum Reserve Geopolitics Oil prices China policy SPR Exchange DUCs Apparent demand Malacca Dilemma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-26-chinatalk-中国用5百万桶进口消失挡掉了伊朗油价末日/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/64c72df8-86f7-11f1-ae50-dfb0b198eafc/image/63e4449937342738bc837a1443333ed6.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:06:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\">ChinaTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0726</span></div>\n<h2>China Cut 5 Million Barrels a Day of Imports — Why the Iran Oil Apocalypse Never Came</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Iran war was once forecast to push oil to $200 a barrel; the disaster never arrived, and the main reason was not the United States but China quietly cutting crude imports by 5 million barrels a day — discretion that can rescue a market, and can just as easily be turned into a geopolitical weapon.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Energy security</span><span class=\"tag\">US-China rivalry</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"No One Confirmed the Doors Were Shut: Institutional Carelessness Was the Real Killer In 1987 the roll-on/roll-off ferry Herald of Free Enterprise capsized with her bow doors open, killing 193 people. The real culprit was not the sleeping crewman but a system that left everyone feeling this was not their job. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales The Doors of Death: The Herald of Free Enterprise Maritime disaster Organizational failure Safety culture Accountability Regulatory lag Swiss cheese model roll-on/roll-off ferry (RoRo) Swiss cheese model corporate manslaughter controlling mind pacing problem\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-24-cautionary-没人确认舱门已关-制度性漫不经心才是元凶/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/c0ae8c6e-22f0-4e9b-ac1c-ae390037ac53/7f5a4714-6b10-4ccf-a424-ae390037ac70/image.jpg?t=1650471153&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">37:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0724</span></div>\n<h2>No One Confirmed the Doors Were Shut: Institutional Carelessness Was the Real Killer</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In 1987 the roll-on/roll-off ferry Herald of Free Enterprise capsized with her bow doors open, killing 193 people. The real culprit was not the sleeping crewman but a system that left everyone feeling this was not their job.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Maritime disaster</span><span class=\"tag\">Organizational failure</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"AI Only Gets You Because Content Engineers Coached It, Line by Line People who used to write the news have turned into AI&#x27;s content engineers, breaking questioning, empathy and a sense of proportion down into training rules — that is where AI&#x27;s ‘understanding’ of you comes from. But training on consensus also leads them to admit: great art will not grow out of this. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E245｜藏在大模型背后的新闻人：GPT们的回复是这样写出来的 Content Engineer Post-training AI Product Design Humanities Career Switch Large Models Generative AI Content Engineer System Prompt Few-shot Example Voice Agent Parasocial Relationship\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-24-sv101-ai的懂你-是内容工程师一句句调教出来的/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/f/f0f20376-8faf-4940-b920-84af6c734e2d/cover.jpg?v=6\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">46:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0724</span></div>\n<h2>AI Only Gets You Because Content Engineers Coached It, Line by Line</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">People who used to write the news have turned into AI&#x27;s content engineers, breaking questioning, empathy and a sense of proportion down into training rules — that is where AI&#x27;s ‘understanding’ of you comes from. But training on consensus also leads them to admit: great art will not grow out of this.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Content Engineer</span><span class=\"tag\">Post-training</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Can a small model that grinds for eight weeks break the foundation-model oligopoly? With a model of 118 billion total parameters and 8 billion active, Poolside argues that persistence and verification behaviour lift coding ability more than raw parameter count does — which is why they believe small open models can break the incumbents&#x27; lock on the future. Latent Space Latent Space Inside the Model Factory — Eiso Kant, Poolside AI Open models Model training Reinforcement learning AI infrastructure AGI Compute RSI / recursive self-improvement MCP / Model Context Protocol FP8/NVFP4 / 8-bit and 4-bit low-precision training DGX Spark / NVIDIA desktop-class AI machine prefill/decode disaggregation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-23-latentspace-poolside-小模型的持久性-比参数量更重要/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/1084089/post/208082176/2e16b76306e11c52de7b41229ff37b1f.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:54:33</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Latent Space</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0723</span></div>\n<h2>Can a small model that grinds for eight weeks break the foundation-model oligopoly?</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">With a model of 118 billion total parameters and 8 billion active, Poolside argues that persistence and verification behaviour lift coding ability more than raw parameter count does — which is why they believe small open models can break the incumbents&#x27; lock on the future.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Open models</span><span class=\"tag\">Model training</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Open models aren&#x27;t closing the gap by distilling — nobody knows how to distill usefully Nathan Lambert takes apart, point by point, the narrative that Chinese open models are just distilled: using Fable/GPT 5.6 as a judge inside the RL stage does not pencil out on cost, and even if you were handed the strongest model&#x27;s reasoning traces for free, the research community still does not know how to convert them into capability. Interconnects Interconnects Open models recap: more on Kimi K3, Qwen 3.8, Xi&#x27;s WAIC speech, distillation, the open-closed gap, and what&#x27;s next Open models Distillation Post-training Compute US-China rivalry Cybersecurity distillation rollout grading model / judge mid-training shadow ban fine-tunability\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-22-interconnects-开源追上前沿不是靠蒸馏-因为没人知道蒸馏怎么才管用/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/48206/post/207969620/4bba19be6ee947d2dc101a9d656ef582.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">49:05</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Interconnects</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0722</span></div>\n<h2>Open models aren&#x27;t closing the gap by distilling — nobody knows how to distill usefully</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Nathan Lambert takes apart, point by point, the narrative that Chinese open models are just distilled: using Fable/GPT 5.6 as a judge inside the RL stage does not pencil out on cost, and even if you were handed the strongest model&#x27;s reasoning traces for free, the research community still does not know how to convert them into capability.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Open models</span><span class=\"tag\">Distillation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"A 28nm Chip Outruns the Leading Edge by 1,000x: Compute-in-Memory Black Magic Without EUV Zhicun Technology (知存科技) turned 28nm Flash into compute-in-memory chips. Because the physics make larger arrays more energy-efficient, efficiency rises as models get bigger — and Transformers are pure upside for the approach. 老石谈芯 老石谈芯 28纳米反超1000倍?不需要EUV的芯片黑魔法：对话知存科技王绍迪 Compute-in-Memory AI Chips Memory Transformer Semiconductor Manufacturing On-Device AI Von Neumann architecture NOR Flash NAND Flash EDA INT4 Universal Memory\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-22-laoshi-模型越大-28纳米存算芯片反而越强/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/Wbu6aGuhW5o/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"老\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">老石谈芯</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0722</span></div>\n<h2>A 28nm Chip Outruns the Leading Edge by 1,000x: Compute-in-Memory Black Magic Without EUV</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Zhicun Technology (<span lang=\"zh\">知存科技</span>) turned 28nm Flash into compute-in-memory chips. Because the physics make larger arrays more energy-efficient, efficiency rises as models get bigger — and Transformers are pure upside for the approach.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute-in-Memory</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Chips</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Three gates still stand between your agent and your money: trust, authorization, merchant readiness Clink and Visa completed the first agent payment, yet the industry is stuck at three gates — trust, authorization and merchant readiness; fiat is running first because consumer protection is mature, while stablecoins are still working on irreversibility. What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道 科技早知道 可以给你的 Agent 发一点零花钱了 | S10E22 AI Agent Agent Payments Payment Protocols Visa Stablecoins Agent Payment ACP UCP / User Choice Protocol VIC / Visa Intelligent Commerce agent enableer chargeback\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-22-whatsnext-智能体支付已落地-但替你花钱还差三道坎/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/4/4931937e-0184-4c61-a658-6b03c254754d/cover.jpg?v=10\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"W\"><span class=\"dur\">41:47</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0722</span></div>\n<h2>Three gates still stand between your agent and your money: trust, authorization, merchant readiness</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Clink and Visa completed the first agent payment, yet the industry is stuck at three gates — trust, authorization and merchant readiness; fiat is running first because consumer protection is mature, while stablecoins are still working on irreversibility.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI Agent</span><span class=\"tag\">Agent Payments</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Embodied AI hasn&#x27;t reached its GPT-1 moment; the block is data that won&#x27;t scale Shen Yujun (沈宇军) of Ant Lingbo (蚂蚁灵波) argues embodied AI has not reached its GPT-1 moment, and the bottleneck is that data has not scaled up: internet data is two orders of magnitude larger than real-robot data, and an ideal pretraining run would start at a million hours. To get there the team rebuilt visual pretraining from scratch and insists on starting from real sensors. 张小珺·商业访谈录 张小珺·商业访谈录 147. 和蚂蚁灵波沈宇军聊：机器人原生基础模型、大脑和本体的关系、预训练与数据scale up、老师汤晓鸥 Embodied AI Robot brains Pretraining Data Ant Lingbo Founding a startup Ego (first-person-view) data WAM (world action model) VLA (vision-language-action model) MOE (mixture of experts)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-22-zhangxiaojun-具身数据没scale-up-gpt-1时刻就还没到/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/FvrM8NWWO-yrGdKP1Dg4Krj68cuM.png?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"张\"><span class=\"dur\">1:52:54</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">张小珺·商业访谈录</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0722</span></div>\n<h2>Embodied AI hasn&#x27;t reached its GPT-1 moment; the block is data that won&#x27;t scale</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Shen Yujun (<span lang=\"zh\">沈宇军</span>) of Ant Lingbo (<span lang=\"zh\">蚂蚁灵波</span>) argues embodied AI has not reached its GPT-1 moment, and the bottleneck is that data has not scaled up: internet data is two orders of magnitude larger than real-robot data, and an ideal pretraining run would start at a million hours. To get there the team rebuilt visual pretraining from scratch and insists on starting from real sensors.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Embodied AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Robot brains</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Yao Song: physical AI is won by systems, not by young geniuses From DeePhi to Orienspace to Striding AI, Yao Song (姚颂) argues that what decides physical AI is not one or two genius algorithms but data, compute, a talent pool and commercial delivery at every milestone — and that the intelligence-first giants may not be the ones who get to pick the fruit. 晚点聊 LateTalk 晚点聊 173: 对话姚颂：深鉴、东方空间、再出发，「天才少年」十年后 Physical AI Embodied intelligence Commercial spaceflight Startup playbook Tsinghua network AI chips WAM (world action model) VLA (vision-language-action model) latent space egocentric data teleoperation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-21-latetalk-姚颂十年三次创业-物理ai的答案不是小天才-而是系统/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/1/19a49f52-28ee-4e25-b8e9-4f0ee70917e0/episodes/8/8cbbc05f-922d-49f2-9c3c-aef3b27cf18a/cover.jpg?v=2\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"晚\"><span class=\"dur\">2:55:18</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">晚点聊 LateTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0721</span></div>\n<h2>Yao Song: physical AI is won by systems, not by young geniuses</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">From DeePhi to Orienspace to Striding AI, Yao Song (<span lang=\"zh\">姚颂</span>) argues that what decides physical AI is not one or two genius algorithms but data, compute, a talent pool and commercial delivery at every milestone — and that the intelligence-first giants may not be the ones who get to pick the fruit.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Physical AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Embodied intelligence</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Open weights now trail closed models by 3-5 months, and that lag is the whole safety margin Kimi K3 compresses the open-versus-closed gap from the 6-9 months people had been arguing over down to 3-5 months, and that lag is the only risk buffer anyone has — heavy-handed regulation of open weights would merely postpone the inevitable while voiding the buffer itself. Interconnects Interconnects Kimi K3: The open-weights escalation Open weights US-China competition Capital efficiency MoE architecture AI policy Kimi Delta Attention (KDA) Attention Residuals (AttnRes) Stable LatentMoE adversarial distillation decelerationist Entity List\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-20-interconnects-开闭源差距只剩-3-5-个月-这层时间差就是全部的安全边际/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/48206/post/207699639/0efacc5bcaac5ab46a3f599e8e22a960.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">20:03</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Interconnects</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0720</span></div>\n<h2>Open weights now trail closed models by 3-5 months, and that lag is the whole safety margin</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Kimi K3 compresses the open-versus-closed gap from the 6-9 months people had been arguing over down to 3-5 months, and that lag is the only risk buffer anyone has — heavy-handed regulation of open weights would merely postpone the inevitable while voiding the buffer itself.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Open weights</span><span class=\"tag\">US-China competition</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Why cross-entropy loss won: it is training a text compressor Cross-entropy loss was selected because it can be proved mathematically to be the only functional form that guarantees the loss is minimized exactly when the model&#x27;s output equals the true distribution of the data — and that turns out to be equivalent to training the model into a text compressor approaching the Shannon limit. Andrej Karpathy Andrej Karpathy But what is cross-entropy? | Compression is Intelligence Part 2 Information theory Cross-entropy Language model training Distillation Compression KL divergence cross-entropy KL divergence (relative entropy) distillation Lagrange multiplier Shannon limit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-16-karpathy-训练语言模型本质上是在训练一个文本压缩器/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/GlYgs6v2YfU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Andrej Karpathy</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0716</span></div>\n<h2>Why cross-entropy loss won: it is training a text compressor</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Cross-entropy loss was selected because it can be proved mathematically to be the only functional form that guarantees the loss is minimized exactly when the model&#x27;s output equals the true distribution of the data — and that turns out to be equivalent to training the model into a text compressor approaching the Shannon limit.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Information theory</span><span class=\"tag\">Cross-entropy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"The naked mole-rat queen rules with a $5 molecule: not urine, a skincare ingredient The signal that suppresses reproduction in naked mole-rats has finally been found: only the queen produces isopropyl myristate. Add it to a colony that has lost its queen and the peace holds; stop, and the succession war breaks out. The same molecule turns up on breastfeeding women. Nature Podcast Nature Podcast ‘Holy grail’ of naked mole-rat research reveals how queens rule naked mole-rats chemical signalling behavioural ecology cognitive science AI reasoning exoplanets isopropyl myristate naked mole-rat super-puff intuitive gamer\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-15-naturepod-裸鼹鼠女王不靠尿液-靠一种5美元分子维持王位/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/61b9f3b71a8cbe675f3cedcb/1768403592746-2c5f9e78-ae15-499a-9d0a-ae6ca82bb9ca.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">22:40</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Nature Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0715</span></div>\n<h2>The naked mole-rat queen rules with a $5 molecule: not urine, a skincare ingredient</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The signal that suppresses reproduction in naked mole-rats has finally been found: only the queen produces isopropyl myristate. Add it to a colony that has lost its queen and the peace holds; stop, and the succession war breaks out. The same molecule turns up on breastfeeding women.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">naked mole-rats</span><span class=\"tag\">chemical signalling</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Two or three assisted-driving suppliers will be left, and the window shuts by year-end Momenta&#x27;s Cao Xudong (曹旭东) argues that assisted driving is like batteries — there is only good and better — so the endgame leaves two or three third-party suppliers in China and three or four globally; the first tier already holds 90% market share, a data flywheel plus mass production is the ticket in, and the next stop is physical AI and home robots. 晚点聊 LateTalk 晚点聊 172: Momenta IPO后再访曹旭东：就是想做没有尽头的AI Assisted driving Robotics Data flywheel Physical AI Momenta Startup management world model RoboVan RoboTruck post-train data scaling\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-15-latetalk-智驾好和更好的行业-只容得下两三家/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/1/19a49f52-28ee-4e25-b8e9-4f0ee70917e0/episodes/8/88bdcde3-ba07-41d3-af81-61edbf4444a8/cover.jpg?v=1\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"晚\"><span class=\"dur\">2:03:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">晚点聊 LateTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0715</span></div>\n<h2>Two or three assisted-driving suppliers will be left, and the window shuts by year-end</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Momenta&#x27;s Cao Xudong (<span lang=\"zh\">曹旭东</span>) argues that assisted driving is like batteries — there is only good and better — so the endgame leaves two or three third-party suppliers in China and three or four globally; the first tier already holds 90% market share, a data flywheel plus mass production is the ticket in, and the next stop is physical AI and home robots.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Assisted driving</span><span class=\"tag\">Robotics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"A black hole is a 100%-efficient power plant; fusion only reaches one percent Winch a brick slowly down to just above the horizon and let go, and 100% of its rest energy can become work far away; chemical burning gets one part in ten billion and fusion one percent, because nuclear reactions never touch the rest mass of protons and neutrons — only gravity does. Dwarkesh Podcast Dwarkesh Adam Brown – A deep but accessible introduction to general relativity General relativity Black holes Energy efficiency AI for science String theory History of physics equivalence principle fictitious / inertial force Schwarzschild radius / event horizon gravitational time dilation spaghettification\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-10-dwarkesh-黑洞是效率-100-的发电厂-聚变只到百分之一/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://apple.dwarkesh-podcast.workers.dev/art/v1/c3Vic3RhY2s6cG9zdDoyMDY0NDU4NDQ.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">1:38:24</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Dwarkesh Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0710</span></div>\n<h2>A black hole is a 100%-efficient power plant; fusion only reaches one percent</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Winch a brick slowly down to just above the horizon and let go, and 100% of its rest energy can become work far away; chemical burning gets one part in ten billion and fusion one percent, because nuclear reactions never touch the rest mass of protons and neutrons — only gravity does.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">General relativity</span><span class=\"tag\">Black holes</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"American Money Controls 11 Premier League Clubs, and Football Is Not the Point US capital now controls 11 Premier League clubs, and it has reached into UEFA commercial rights, broadcast distribution and the financing of player transfers; with media-rights income at its ceiling, it keeps playing by pushing valuations up and rolling assets through evergreen funds. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E243｜特朗普“缓刑”红牌之外，美国资本如何硬控全球足坛 Sports Investing Premier League US Capital Football Business Leveraged Buyouts Leveraged Buyout Asset Securitization Evergreen Fund Super League Matchday Revenue\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-10-sv101-美国资本硬控足坛-不只买队-还在收租/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/f/f0f20376-8faf-4940-b920-84af6c734e2d/cover.jpg?v=6\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">1:16:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0710</span></div>\n<h2>American Money Controls 11 Premier League Clubs, and Football Is Not the Point</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">US capital now controls 11 Premier League clubs, and it has reached into UEFA commercial rights, broadcast distribution and the financing of player transfers; with media-rights income at its ceiling, it keeps playing by pushing valuations up and rolling assets through evergreen funds.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Sports Investing</span><span class=\"tag\">Premier League</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Two ways to live in short drama: scale protects the capital, content runs on relationships Short drama has two survival modes: the scale mode runs on capital safety and the near-certain returns of 300 titles a month, the content mode on character relationships that determine motive; both sides think AI cannot replace a live actor&#x27;s micro-expressions for now. 乱翻书 乱翻书 269. 卷规模 VS 卷创作：真人短剧的两种生存模式 Live-action shorts Capacity management Content method AI disruption Female-audience hits Interactive film games RY (input-to-output ratio, return multiple) DIT (Digital Imaging Technician) Zhanshaxian (斩杀线), the kill line Jinshouzhi (金手指), the protagonist&#x27;s cheat power\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-09-luanfanshu-月产-300-部短剧不靠灵感-靠本金安全与人物关系/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/FiCrZ5GF4_Z3YonxYT7pBH4HZkbr.jpg?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"乱\"><span class=\"dur\">1:11:37</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">乱翻书</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0709</span></div>\n<h2>Two ways to live in short drama: scale protects the capital, content runs on relationships</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Short drama has two survival modes: the scale mode runs on capital safety and the near-certain returns of 300 titles a month, the content mode on character relationships that determine motive; both sides think AI cannot replace a live actor&#x27;s micro-expressions for now.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Live-action shorts</span><span class=\"tag\">Capacity management</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Self-evolving AI could close the loop in six months, but the model will quietly drift The inflection point for RSI is models becoming capable of long-horizon tasks. Apodex&#x27;s chief scientist says the self-evolution loop could close in as little as six months, but recursive drift and the model&#x27;s taste will need human gatekeeping for a long time yet. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E242｜最快半年AI跑通自进化？与陈天桥首席科学家聊聊硅谷模型必争之地 AI self-evolution RSI Long-horizon tasks Agent teams Model taste Research automation RSI (Recursive Self-Improvement) Recursive Drift Heavy Duty Solver Discovery Model Agent Team\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-06-sv101-ai最快半年跑通自进化-验证与品味是最后门槛/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/f/f0f20376-8faf-4940-b920-84af6c734e2d/cover.jpg?v=6\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">1:10:54</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0706</span></div>\n<h2>Self-evolving AI could close the loop in six months, but the model will quietly drift</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The inflection point for RSI is models becoming capable of long-horizon tasks. Apodex&#x27;s chief scientist says the self-evolution loop could close in as little as six months, but recursive drift and the model&#x27;s taste will need human gatekeeping for a long time yet.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI self-evolution</span><span class=\"tag\">RSI</span>\n</div></div></a>"]